@database "lessons_learned"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: lessons_learned.guide 1.0 (29.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Lessons Learned"
@{h1}Lessons Learned

What an agent has learned and should keep doing -- "check every date
against the timeline", "run the targeted tests before a commit" -- kept
across sessions, per agent. An agent stores lessons with its tool, teaches
them to another agent, and confirms or contradicts them as it goes; each
lesson carries a confidence that the evidence moves. An optional hook puts
the active lessons of an agent in front of its model, another one lets an
LLM pick lessons out of the conversation as it goes on. In the
@{b}Lessons Learned@{ub} panel you review, activate, edit, merge and clean
up the lessons of every agent.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Lessons Learned panel with the lessons of several agents"}

@{code}
For users
  @{"  The Lessons Learned panel  " link panel}

For agents and developers
  @{"  The lessons_learned tool  " link tool}
  @{"  Confidence, evidence and duplicates  " link rules}
  @{"  The inject_lessons hook  " link inject}
  @{"  The extract_lessons hook  " link extract}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node panel "The Lessons Learned panel"
@{h1}The Lessons Learned panel

Open it from the launcher (@{b}Context & memory@{ub}, "Lessons Learned").
Lessons belong to agents, not to chat sessions: the panel shows the
lessons of every agent, whatever is open in the chat.

@{image docs/panel.png "The Lessons Learned panel"}

@{h2}What you see

@{bullet}Six figures: all lessons, how many are active, draft, inactive and
archived, and how many agents have lessons. The agent filter narrows the
first five to that agent.
@{bullet}Filters by agent, status and category, and the order: by priority
(then confidence), by confidence, by evidence, newest first or recently
updated. An agent or category you filter for stays in its menu, also once
no lesson has it any more.
@{bullet}The lessons, 50 to a page with @{b}Previous@{ub} and
@{b}Next@{ub}: title, text, id and tags; agent, category, priority,
confidence (green from 0.7, red below 0.4), status, evidence, applications
(how often the hook put it in front of the model) and source --
@{i}Manual@{ui}, @{i}Cross-agent@{ui} (taught), @{i}Reflection@{ui} (stored
by the agent itself) or @{i}Auto@{ui} (extracted).

The panel reloads every 30 seconds; the menu next to the reload button sets
another interval or turns it off. If the lessons cannot be loaded, the
error takes the place of the figures and no stale list stays.

@{h2}Search

The search box finds lessons by meaning -- "dates" finds "Check every date
against the timeline". It searches every status unless the status filter
names one, and the agent and category filters narrow it too. Up to 50
lessons come back, the closest first, with their similarity; a click on a
column head sorts them. @{b}Clear@{ub} goes back to the list.

@{h2}What you can do with a lesson

@{table}
Button | Shown on | Does
Activate | a draft | makes it active, so the hook uses it; refused if it is no longer a draft
Edit | every lesson | opens it, loaded afresh, in the editor
Delete | every lesson | removes it with its evidence, after asking
@{body}

@{b}New lesson@{ub} opens the editor empty: the agent of the agent filter,
category general, active, source manual, priority 5, confidence 0.8. The
editor has every field -- agent, category, title (200 characters), text
(2000), status, source, priority 1 to 10, confidence 0 to 1 and tags,
comma-separated. Changing the agent moves the lesson to that agent. A save
sends every field; the confidence you set holds until the next evidence
(see @{" Confidence " link rules}). When a save worked but the search index
could not take the lesson, a warning says so: it is listed, but search and
the duplicate check miss it until the index works again.

When the server refuses -- the lesson is gone, no longer a draft, or the
agent has reached its lesson limit -- the panel shows the reason. After
@{b}Activate@{ub} or @{b}Delete@{ub} the list is loaded anew either way; a
refused save keeps the editor open with what you typed, and the list as it
was.

@{h2}Consolidate

@{b}Consolidate@{ub} merges lessons that say the same. Lessons of one agent,
archived ones left out, at least as similar as the threshold (empty: the plugin's
@{tt}dedup_similarity_threshold@{utt}, 0.82) form a group; an LLM judges
each group and writes the merged title and text. The lesson it keeps gets
the evidence and applications of the others, which are deleted.

@{bullet}Leave the agent empty for every agent.
@{bullet}@{b}Dry run@{ub}, on at first, only shows what would be merged.
@{bullet}A bar shows the progress; the result lists each group --
@{i}Merged@{ui} (which lesson stays, which went), @{i}Would merge@{ui},
@{i}Skipped@{ui} with the reason, @{i}Kept separate@{ui} -- and the agents
whose lessons could not be compared at all.
@{bullet}One merge runs at a time; a second is refused. A merge goes on
when you close the panel, a dry run stops.

@{h2}Clean up

@{b}Clean up@{ub} deletes lessons by filter: agent, status, older than a
number of days (by creation), evidence at most, confidence at most. A
lesson must match every filter set. @{b}Preview@{ub} lists the matches;
@{b}Delete@{ub} then removes only those, after asking -- a lesson that
came to match since is not touched. Changing a filter drops the preview.
Without any filter the server refuses.
@endnode

@node tool "The lessons_learned tool"
@{h1}The lessons_learned tool

The plugin gives an agent one tool, named like the plugin instance
(@{tt}lessons_learned@{utt} in the default setup). Every call names an
@{tt}operation@{utt}; without one it lists. Lessons belong to agents, not
sessions: an agent's lessons are those stored under its name, and ids
count per agent -- @{tt}coder_les_001@{utt}, @{tt}coder_les_002@{utt},
...

@{h2}Operations

@{table}
operation | Needs | Does
store | title, content | a new draft lesson of the calling agent; see @{" duplicates " link rules}
search | query | the active lessons closest in meaning
list | -- | lessons of every status, filtered and sorted
update | lesson_id | changes the fields given
confirm | lesson_id | records evidence for or against a lesson; its confidence is calculated anew
teach | target_agent, title, content | a new draft lesson of another agent
delete | lesson_id | removes the lesson with its evidence
@{body}

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Parameter | Used by | Meaning
title | store, teach, update | up to 200 characters
content | store, teach, update | up to 2000 characters; with the title, what search compares
category | store, teach, update; list, search | any name, the schema offers nine; store and teach without it: general. For list and search a filter
priority | store, teach, update | 1 to 10, rounded to a whole number; store and teach without it: 5
tags | store, teach, update | a list, or one comma-separated string; update replaces them
query | search | what to look for, in words
lesson_id | update, confirm, delete | an id an answer returned
status | update; list | draft, active, inactive or archived; for list a filter
confidence | update | 0 to 1; holds until the next evidence
evidence_type | confirm | confirm (default), contradict or neutral
description | confirm | a note kept with the evidence
target_agent | teach | the agent the lesson is for
agent_name | list, search | whose lessons; without it the calling agent's
limit | list, search | 1 to 100; without it list 20, search 10
sort_by | list | priority (default, then confidence), confidence, evidence, created, updated, applied -- highest or newest first
@{body}

A lesson stored by the tool is a @{b}draft@{ub}: listed, and seen by the
duplicate check, but not found by search nor put in front of the model
until it is active -- by @{b}Activate@{ub} in the panel or
@{tt}update@{utt} with @{tt}status: active@{utt}. There is no offset: a
list shows at most 100 lessons, the filters narrow it. Any agent can
update, confirm or delete any lesson whose id it names.

@{h2}Answers

@{bullet}store, teach: @{tt}status: stored@{utt}, the new
@{tt}lesson_id@{utt}, @{tt}agent_name@{utt}, @{tt}title@{utt} and
@{tt}lesson_status: draft@{utt}. When a similar lesson exists nothing is
stored: the answer is the evidence added to that one, with
@{tt}dedup_action@{utt} (@{tt}confirm@{utt} or @{tt}merge@{utt}) and
@{tt}similar_to@{utt}, its id.
@{bullet}search: @{tt}results@{utt} -- whole lessons with a
@{tt}similarity@{utt} from 0 to 1, the closest first -- @{tt}count@{utt}
and @{tt}query@{utt}.
@{bullet}list: @{tt}lessons@{utt}, @{tt}total@{utt} (all that match),
@{tt}limit@{utt}, @{tt}offset@{utt}.
@{bullet}update: @{tt}status: updated@{utt}, @{tt}updated_fields@{utt}.
@{bullet}confirm: @{tt}status: evidence_added@{utt},
@{tt}evidence_type@{utt}, @{tt}new_confidence@{utt},
@{tt}evidence_count@{utt}. The same kind of evidence for the same lesson
from the same session is kept once, and the session a lesson came from
does not confirm it: either answers @{tt}status: evidence_exists@{utt} with
the figures unchanged.
@{bullet}delete: @{tt}status: deleted@{utt}.
@{bullet}What still worked but could not be done completely comes as
@{tt}warnings@{utt}: a lesson stored without the duplicate check, or left
out of the search index; agents whose lessons a search could not reach.
@{bullet}A refusal is @{tt}{"error": "..."}@{utt}: a parameter missing, a
title over 200 characters, a priority outside 1 to 10, a lesson id not
found, the agent's lesson limit reached, a search that could not run at
all. A status or confidence out of range on update fails with the
database's message.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"operation": "store", "title": "Run the targeted tests before a commit", "content": "The whole suite takes twenty minutes; run the tests of the module you changed.", "category": "workflow", "priority": 8}
{"operation": "update", "lesson_id": "coder_les_004", "status": "active"}
{"operation": "search", "query": "which tests to run"}
{"operation": "confirm", "lesson_id": "coder_les_004", "description": "The targeted run caught a broken import"}
{"operation": "teach", "target_agent": "reviewer", "title": "Run the targeted tests before a commit", "content": "..."}
@{body}
@endnode

@node rules "Confidence, evidence and duplicates"
@{h1}Confidence, evidence and duplicates

@{h2}Confidence

A lesson starts with a confidence by its source: 0.8 made in the panel
(the editor sets it), 0.6 taught, 0.5 stored by the agent, 0.4 extracted.
Every piece of evidence calculates it anew from that start and the
difference of confirming and contradicting evidence; neutral evidence is
counted, but moves nothing. A session gives a lesson at most one evidence
of each kind -- a lesson confirmed twice in one conversation, or a
conversation read twice, counts once -- and the session a lesson came from
does not confirm it. Each confirmation adds less than the one
before: an agent's own lesson (0.5) is at 0.58 after one, 0.65 after three,
0.71 after ten, never above 0.75; contradictions lower it the same way,
never below half the start. A confidence set by hand holds until the next
evidence.

Evidence comes from @{tt}confirm@{utt}, from a store or teach of a lesson
that already exists, and from the extraction finding a lesson again. A
merge moves the evidence of the lessons merged away to the one it keeps --
where two came from the same session, one of a kind stays -- adds one
confirming evidence per lesson merged away, and keeps the highest
confidence of the group, without calculating anew.

@{h2}Duplicates

@{tt}store@{utt} and @{tt}teach@{utt} compare the new lesson with the
lessons of the agent it is for, in every status. At a similarity of
@{tt}dedup_similarity_threshold@{utt} (0.82) or more nothing is stored; the
closest lesson gets a confirming evidence instead. From
@{tt}exact_duplicate_threshold@{utt} (0.95) the answer says
@{tt}dedup_action: confirm@{utt}, below it @{tt}merge@{utt} -- both do the
same. When the check cannot run (the embedding model is missing), the
lesson is stored and the answer warns that it was not checked.

@{h2}Status

@{bullet}draft -- stored or taught by an agent, or extracted; not used.
@{bullet}active -- found by search and put in front of the model by the
hook.
@{bullet}inactive, archived -- kept, but not used. Archived lessons do not
count toward an agent's limit.

A status changes by hand -- the panel, or @{tt}update@{utt}. Evidence
changes it only in one direction: an inactive lesson whose confidence is
0.4 or more after new evidence becomes active again.
@endnode

@node inject "The inject_lessons hook"
@{h1}The inject_lessons hook

@{tt}inject_lessons@{utt} runs before each LLM call and puts the agent's
active lessons in front of its model. It is off until an agent switches it
on.

@{h2}What the model gets

A message at the end of the history, from the plugin (a
@{tt}developer@{utt} turn): the agent's active lessons with a confidence
of at least @{tt}min_confidence@{utt}, the most evidence first, then the
highest confidence, then priority; at most @{tt}max_lessons@{utt}. They are
grouped by category, each text cut at 300 characters, and the block ends
before it would pass @{tt}max_tokens@{utt} (counted as four characters a
token). The mark before a lesson shows its confidence: ● from 0.8, ◐ from
0.5, ○ below.

@{code markdown}
## LESSONS LEARNED
The following are verified lessons from past sessions. Apply them where relevant to improve quality and consistency.

### Domain Knowledge
- ● **Check every date against the timeline** [P8]
  Dates drift between chapters; check each one against the timeline.
  Tags: continuity, dates
### Workflow
- ◐ **Run the targeted tests before a commit** [P7]
  The whole suite takes twenty minutes.
@{body}

The message is added only when it differs from the last one the hook
added; otherwise nothing changes. Every lesson in the block counts as
applied at every LLM call, also when nothing was added -- the block from
before still stands. An agent without active lessons gets nothing.

@{h2}Switching it on

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  hooks:
    enabled: true
    overrides:
      lessons_learned.inject_lessons:
        enabled: true
        max_lessons: 10
        min_confidence: 0.5
@{body}

@{h2}Settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
max_lessons | 15 | how many lessons the block may hold
max_tokens | 1500 | the size of the block, about four characters a token
min_confidence | 0.3 | lessons below it stay out
include_categories | every category | a list: only these
exclude_categories | none | a list: not these
@{body}

The settings are read only from the agent's override, as above; the
plugin's server entry does not set them.
@endnode

@node extract "The extract_lessons hook"
@{h1}The extract_lessons hook

@{tt}extract_lessons@{utt} runs at the end of every request the agent
answers, with the conversation so far, and asks an LLM which lessons the
part it has not read yet holds: corrections, preferences, domain
knowledge, quality and error patterns -- not one-off facts or how to use
the tools. It is off until an agent switches it on, and it changes nothing
in the conversation.

@{h2}What it does

@{bullet}It reads only the text of messages a person or the assistant
wrote: what the user wrote and what the assistant answered. Not the system
prompt, not tool calls or results, and nothing a plugin or the loop put
into the conversation -- among them the lessons block of
@{" inject_lessons " link inject}.
@{bullet}It remembers, per session and agent, the last message it read --
by its text, the message before it and their timestamps, not by position
-- and next time reads the messages after it. It waits until there are at
least @{tt}min_turns@{utt} of them -- with the default 5, about every
third request -- and 100 characters of text.
@{bullet}One reading takes up to 8000 characters; a single message longer
than that is shortened to fit. Readings follow each other until fewer
than @{tt}min_turns@{utt} unread messages are left, within 15 seconds a
request: a reading starts only while the longest one so far still fits.
What is left then is read after the next request. If the message just
remembered cannot be found again, the readings stop for that request
rather than read the same messages twice. A second request of the same
session while the readings run leaves them to the first.
@{bullet}The session is free for the next message only after the hook is
done: with extraction on, the user may wait up to about 15 seconds more
after an answer, one LLM call per reading.
@{bullet}When the remembered message is gone -- a compaction replaced the
history -- it reads every written message that is left. The compaction's
summary is not among them: it was put in by a plugin.
@{bullet}After each reading the LLM answered, even with no lesson, it
remembers the last message read -- also when text stands around the JSON,
or a comma before a closing bracket. Not when the answer was empty, no
JSON, or cut off and had to be mended, and not when a lesson could not be checked
for duplicates: then the same messages are read again after the next
request. While the duplicate check cannot run at all (the embedding model
is missing), the LLM is not asked.
@{bullet}Of the lessons it names, the first
@{tt}max_lessons_per_session@{utt} are taken. Each is checked for
@{" duplicates " link rules}: a known one gets a confirming evidence, a new
one is stored as a draft, or active with @{tt}auto_approve@{utt}, source
@{i}Auto@{ui}. A lesson the duplicate check could not check, or the store
refused (the agent's limit), is skipped.

The hook's own timeout is 30 seconds; the readings keep within their 15.

@{h2}Switching it on

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  hooks:
    enabled: true
    overrides:
      lessons_learned.extract_lessons:
        enabled: true
        min_turns: 6
        extraction_llm_profile: "or-deepseek-flash"
@{body}

@{h2}Settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
min_turns | 5 | messages a person or the assistant wrote, not yet read, before the LLM is asked
max_lessons_per_session | 5 | how many of the lessons named are taken, per reading
auto_approve | false | true: new lessons are stored active, not as drafts
extraction_llm_profile | the server's llm_profile | the LLM profile that extracts
@{body}

Read from the agent's override; only the profile falls back to the
plugin's server entry.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The tool

The tool description and every parameter's description come from the
plugin's @{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}. A refused call answers
@{tt}{"error": "Both 'title' and 'content' are required."}@{utt},
@{tt}{"error": "'title' is longer than 200 characters."}@{utt},
@{tt}{"error": "Lesson 'coder_les_009' not found."}@{utt},
@{tt}{"error": "Lesson limit (500) reached for agent 'coder'. Archive or
delete older lessons."}@{utt} and the like. In the chat, the call's status
line ends with the result: "Lesson stored: coder_les_004", "Not stored:
similar to coder_les_001, evidence added", "Found 3 lessons", "Retrieved
12 lessons", "Evidence added: confirm (confidence: 0.583)", "Lesson taught
to editor: editor_les_002".

@{h2}Tokens and cache

Tool answers are ordinary tool results: appended, nothing earlier changes.
@{tt}list@{utt} and @{tt}search@{utt} return whole lessons, each text up to
2000 characters; a small @{tt}limit@{utt} keeps an answer short. The hook
appends its block at the end of the history and only when it changed; it
never rewrites the system prompt or an earlier message. But a changed
block is a whole new block: new evidence can reorder the lessons or change
a mark, and each such change appends the full list again.

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}A lesson the agent stores is a draft: its own search does not find
it, and the hook does not use it, until it is activated.
@{bullet}Evidence never makes a lesson inactive: its confidence cannot fall
below half its start, and the switch waits for 0.2. It does make an
inactive lesson active again -- also one a person set inactive.
@{bullet}Messages still waiting for @{tt}min_turns@{utt} company -- up to
@{tt}min_turns@{utt} minus one -- are lost when a compaction removes them
before the next reading. Closing that would need the extraction to run
before the compaction.
@{bullet}An answer that keeps failing is asked for again after every
request.
@{bullet}"Applications" counts LLM calls, not sessions.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

The plugin is on in the default configuration:

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    lessons_learned:
      type: lessons_learned
      enabled: true
      database_path: "data/lessons_learned/lessons.db"
      max_lessons_per_agent: 500
      dedup_similarity_threshold: 0.82
      exact_duplicate_threshold: 0.95
      llm_profile: "or-deepseek-flash"
      consolidation_llm_profile: "or-deepseek-flash"
@{body}

An agent sees the tool when its allowlist names it:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  tools:
    allowed:
      - "+lessons_learned/*"
@{body}

Search, the duplicate check and consolidation need a vector store
(@{tt}chromadb@{utt}, or @{tt}sqlite-vec@{utt}) and the embedding model
all-MiniLM-L6-v2, made locally. Without the model lessons are still
stored, listed and edited, with a warning; search answers an error. Once
the model is back, the lessons it missed are indexed by the next search or
store of that agent.

@{h2}Server settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
database_path | lessons_learned/lessons.db in the data directory | the SQLite database
max_lessons_per_agent | 200 | lessons an agent may have, archived ones not counted; a store beyond it is refused
dedup_similarity_threshold | 0.82 | similarity from which a new lesson is a duplicate; also the consolidation's default
exact_duplicate_threshold | 0.95 | from here a duplicate is reported as confirm, not merge
llm_profile | turbo | the LLM profile of the extraction, unless the agent sets one
consolidation_llm_profile | turbo | the LLM profile that judges a consolidation
@{body}

Lessons, their evidence, the applications and a log of the extractions
live in the database; the search index lies beside it in
@{tt}vectors/@{utt}.
@endnode
